The barbarian was started as a side project, as my Wizard turned out to
be too lucky. The Wizard started with a book of identify. And has done
all the prereqs before Medusa including most of the spellbooks, amulet
of lifesaving and a good AC plus resistances. And he is now polypiling
in Fort Ludios. I was feeling that it was all too easy. And put the
Wizard in for a break. I felt an YAAD or YASD was about to happen.

Now, I start the Barbarian to have a break from the spellcasting and
find an early altar. Saccing gives me Cleaver. An ok weapon that was my
main weapon for the rest of the game. But then I stumble upon my unlucky
healer which died the turn after he got a wish. So whaddyaknow? An
unused gdsm just for me! Cursed, but that's not a problem. And a cloak
of protection, too. Now, I hate soko so much that I tend to leave that
as long as I can. I sac some more and gain levels. Eat wraith corpses
and gain even more levels.

Then today, I log in to see it's full moon. And I'm lucky. Oh, yeah. I
run down to the minetown. Picking up the candles. I allready had a bag
that I suspected was a BoH. Finding a cheap scroll which I blessed
helped me to identify my entire inventory including the BoH. Lucky
indeed.  Greased it, blessed it and went down to the bottom. Now... I
find a grey  stone. "Thump". Not picking up that one. Then I blind
myself and see the mimics inside the walls. And you guessed it. All
mimiced a grey stone, but there was none left after I removed them. Only
gems. Lucky? Naaah. Smashed down the doors to all the secret rooms, but
no luckstone to be found.

I run up to my altar and box-o-stash and stash the gems and everything
else I didn't need right now. Sacced and ate some more and gained a few
levels, fire and cold resistance. Plus enabled me to pray just incase.
Now I travel down past the oracle and head for soko. I leave my large
dog behind. The soko goes without too much hassle, until I reach the
end. I try to stay away from the opening to the large room, and kill
each monster coming my way. Then, when there are only a few left, I
enter the room.

I was zapped by a wand of disintegration.

... and it bounces.

Both the cloak and the gdsm went up in smoke, changing my ac from -8 to
+3. I didn't know the dragon armor could be dested at all. But I learned
my lesson today (Yet Another Lesson). The icing on the cake was ending
up as a roadkill when I was overrun by a mumak while a zombie blocked
the door. DYWYPI?

Now I wonder what kind of YAAD/YASD that will end my wizard... I don't
think I dare to play him for another while.

